[SE00104] 📐 GEOMETRY CRIME [Line 7]: Tried to '.+' a 'f32[3, 4]' with a 'f32[5]'. Counting from the right, axis 1 has 4 against 5, and neither is 1.
  --> bad_tensor_shapes.splat:7:6
   |
 7 | x := A .+ B
   |      ^^^^^^
  Fix: Broadcasting lines the shapes up on the right: each pair of dimensions must be equal, or one of them must be 1.

[SE00104] 📐 GEOMETRY CRIME [Line 8]: Tried to '+' a 'f32[3, 4]' with a 'f32[2, 4]'. Axis 0 is 3 on the left and 2 on the right.
  --> bad_tensor_shapes.splat:8:6
   |
 8 | y := A + C
   |      ^^^^^
  Fix: '+' needs identical shapes; use '.+' to broadcast, or reshape one side.

[SE00106] 🤹 WRONG TOOL [Line 9]: '*' has no idea what to do with a 'f32[3, 4]' and a 'f32[3, 4]'.
  --> bad_tensor_shapes.splat:9:6
   |
 9 | z := A * A
   |      ^^^^^
  Fix: A tensor times a tensor is ambiguous: did you mean '.*' (elementwise) or '@' (matrix product)?

[SE00106] 🤹 WRONG TOOL [Line 10]: '/' has no idea what to do with a 'f32[3, 4]' and a 'f32[3, 4]'.
  --> bad_tensor_shapes.splat:10:6
    |
 10 | w := A / A
    |      ^^^^^
  Fix: A tensor divided by a tensor is ambiguous: did you mean './' (elementwise)?

[SE00106] 🤹 WRONG TOOL [Line 11]: '.+' has no idea what to do with a 'f32[3, 4]' and a 'f64[3, 4]'.
  --> bad_tensor_shapes.splat:11:6
    |
 11 | v := A .+ D
    |      ^^^^^^
  Fix: The element types differ ('f32' versus 'f64'). Convert one side explicitly, for example f32(B).

[SE00106] 🤹 WRONG TOOL [Line 12]: '<' has no idea what to do with a 'f32[3, 4]' and a 'f32[2, 4]'.
  --> bad_tensor_shapes.splat:12:6
    |
 12 | u := A < C
    |      ^^^^^
  Fix: A tensor has no single order. Reduce it first: 'max(A) < 3.0', 'min(A) >= 0.0', or compare elements with indexing.

[SE00104] 📐 GEOMETRY CRIME [Line 13]: Tried to shove a 'f32[3, 4]' into a 'f32[3, 3]' slot. The shapes disagree (axis 1 is 4 but 3 was expected).
  --> bad_tensor_shapes.splat:13:16
    |
 13 | t::f32[3, 3] = A
    |                ^
  Fix: Pass a tensor of shape f32[3, 3], or declare the slot with '?' for the dimension that varies.

[SE00104] 📐 GEOMETRY CRIME [Line 14]: Tried to index a 'f32[3, 4]' with 3 indices, but it only has 2 axes.
  --> bad_tensor_shapes.splat:14:6
    |
 14 | s := A[1, 2, 3]
    |      ^^^^^^^^^^
  Fix: Use at most one index per axis.

[SE00104] 📐 GEOMETRY CRIME [Line 15]: Tried to stack a 'f32[1]' row onto 'f32[2]' rows. The rows of a tensor literal must all have the same shape.
  --> bad_tensor_shapes.splat:15:18
    |
 15 | r := f32[[1, 2], [3]]
    |                  ^^^
  Fix: Make every row the same length, or build a List instead.

[SE00104] 📐 GEOMETRY CRIME [Line 16]: Tried to reshape a 'f32[3, 4]' (12 elements) into a 'f32[5, 5]' (25 elements).
  --> bad_tensor_shapes.splat:16:6
    |
 16 | q := reshape(A, 5, 5)
    |      ^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^
  Fix: A reshape keeps the element count: the new dimensions must multiply to the same number.

[SE00002] 🤨 WAIT WHAT [Line 17]: Found 'a 'f32' index' where I wanted an integer index, a range such as 0..3, or ':' for a whole axis. The parser is concerned.
  --> bad_tensor_shapes.splat:17:8
    |
 17 | p := A[0.5]
    |        ^^^
  Fix: Replace 'a 'f32' index' with an integer index, a range such as 0..3, or ':' for a whole axis.

